\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stan Alcorn is an investigative reporter, editor and audio maker. For the last four years, he has been reporting from Colombia and elsewhere in Latin America for APM's Marketplace, BBC's Witness History, NPR's Planet Money, PRX's The World, Audubon Magazine, Rest of World, and the Radio Ambulante Studios podcast La Ruta del Sol. This work was supported by the Alicia Patterson Foundation, the McGraw Center for Business Journalism at CUNY, and the Earth Journalism Network.
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 Previously, Stan was senior reporter-producer at Reveal, the weekly, narrative, national public radio show of investigative reporting. In his seven years there, his stories helped motivate changes in law; were taught in university classrooms; and won honors including a Peabody Award, an NABJ Salute to Excellence Award, a Best of the West Award, multiple Online Journalism Awards and Society for Professional Journalists awards, and a finalist designation for the Livingston Award for Young Journalists.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 Prior to Reveal, he was a staff reporter at Marketplace, WNYC and Fast Company; helped launch new shows at Slate, Marketplace and WNYC; and helped create the website that\'92s now GCJT.org, an online resource for journalists who cover violence.
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 Stan has also taught workshops on radio storytelling at UCLA and City Bureau, and once gave a talk at the Third Coast International Audio Festival about why radio storytelling is bad, actually.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 If you were a radio producer on the Internet in 2014, you may be familiar with an article he wrote for Digg.com about why audio doesn\'92t (usually) go viral. Still true.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 You can contact him at stan dot alcorn at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://stanalcorn.com/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 stanalcorn.com}}}